<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy | Zelux"
  description="How Zelux (Kaden Ekuma Bokome, UK sole trader) collects, uses and protects personal data under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated="26 November 2026"
>
  <p>This notice explains how your personal data is handled when you use <strong>zelux.co.uk</strong>, book a call, or send an enquiry.</p>

  <h2>Who controls your data</h2>
  <p>The data controller is <strong>Kaden Ekuma Bokome</strong>, trading as <strong>Zelux</strong>, a UK sole trader based in Hampshire, United Kingdom. Zelux is not VAT registered.</p>
  <p>Contact for anything privacy-related: <a href="mailto:kaden@zelux.co.uk">kaden@zelux.co.uk</a>.</p>

  <h2>What data is collected</h2>
  <h3>Enquiry form</h3>
  <p>If you use the form on the booking page, your name, email address, business or website (if given) and message reach me by email at kaden@zelux.co.uk. Depending on how the form is set up, it either opens your own email app with the message ready to send, or is delivered through <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, a form-delivery service.</p>
  <h3>Call bookings</h3>
  <p>Calls are arranged by email. If an online booking calendar is offered on this site and you use it, your name, email address, chosen time and any notes you add are processed by <strong>Cal.com</strong> and added to my calendar, along with a video-call link.</p>
  <h3>Site usage</h3>
  <p>The hosting provider (<strong>Vercel</strong>) keeps standard server logs, such as IP address, browser type and pages requested, for security and reliability. If analytics are enabled, they use Vercel Web Analytics, which counts page views in aggregate without cookies and without identifying you, and Vercel Speed Insights, which records anonymous page-speed measurements.</p>

  <h2>Why it's used, and the lawful basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry and prepare a proposal you've asked for: <em>steps prior to entering a contract</em> (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(b)).</li>
    <li>To deliver work once we've agreed a project: <em>performance of a contract</em> (Article 6(1)(b)).</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure and working: <em>legitimate interests</em> (Article 6(1)(f)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your data is never sold, and it's never used for marketing lists you haven't asked to join.</p>

  <h2>Who it's shared with</h2>
  <p>Only the service providers that make the site work: Web3Forms (form delivery, when used), Cal.com (bookings, when used), Vercel (hosting), Zoho Mail (email) and Google (calendar). Some of these providers may process data outside the UK. Where they do, they rely on recognised safeguards such as the UK International Data Transfer Addendum or adequacy regulations.</p>

  <h2>How long it's kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Enquiries that don't become a project: deleted within 12 months.</li>
    <li>Client and contract records: kept for 6 years, to meet HMRC record-keeping requirements for sole traders.</li>
    <li>Server logs: kept for the provider's standard short retention period.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to access the data held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict how it's used, and to data portability. Email <a href="mailto:kaden@zelux.co.uk">kaden@zelux.co.uk</a> and I'll respond within one month.</p>
  <p>If you're unhappy with how your data has been handled, you can complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>. I'd appreciate the chance to put it right first.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this notice changes, the updated version will be posted here with a new date.</p>
</Legal>
